Add the PEP 517 build-system table

preprocess_cancellation 0.2.1 ships a poetry pyproject.toml that has no
[build-system] table, and the sdist carries no setup.py or setup.cfg.
PEP 517 front-ends therefore fall back to the legacy backend
setuptools.build_meta:__legacy__, which does not fail loudly: it builds a
wheel named preprocess_cancellation-0.0.0 with stub metadata and no
console_scripts entry point.

Declare the poetry-core backend the project actually uses, so the wheel
carries the real version, metadata and entry point.

Upstream added the table after this release; 0.2.1 is the version
Moonraker v0.9.3 pins.

--- a/pyproject.toml
+++ b/pyproject.toml
@@ -39,3 +39,7 @@
 
 [tool.coverage.run]
 branch = true
+
+[build-system]
+requires = ["poetry-core>=1.0.0"]
+build-backend = "poetry.core.masonry.api"
